Ticket #4471 merged **412 unique reports**, but its reports describe two independent date
failures. Grouping uses the tenant's locale and booking form rather than the intake tag.

<Callout>
The existing parser ticket covers the larger group. The booking-v3 hint needs its own ticket.
</Callout>

## Problems found

### Parser reads day-first dates as month-first

The shared parser reads every date month first. In a day-first tenant, a date such as 4/7 is
interpreted as 7 April instead of 4 July. This group contains **379 reports**.

### booking-v3 gives day-first tenants a month-first hint

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. Its users type dates in that order, while the tenant expects
day-first input. This is a separate form-hint failure affecting **33 reports**.

## Evidence from #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Resolution

Work on #4471 is complete. The two follow-up tickets close with this documented split, so the
desk retains the evidence for both failures without keeping duplicate work open.

